# Frontend standards

- TypeScript strict mode, no any. Derive API types from the backend OpenAPI schema or one shared types module.
- Every view implements loading, empty and error states. Show backend error messages.
- No dead buttons. A control either works or is disabled with a tooltip: "Planned" or "Unavailable: <reason from /api/health>".
- Show only values returned by the API. No hardcoded sample results in components. Demo data exists only in test fixtures and is labelled as such.
- Progress indicators come only from real job progress fields. Otherwise use an indeterminate spinner.
- No confidence meters unless the backend returns a documented, calibrated quantity.
- Next to every number show its unit and an origin badge (Experimental record, Database-reported, Calculated, ML prediction). Every result view has a Limitations panel.
- Isolate the 3D viewer in one wrapper component. Dispose it on unmount. Chain and residue selections come from API data.
- Accessibility: labelled inputs, visible keyboard focus, aria-live for job status, adequate contrast, never colour alone.
- Responsive down to 375 px width.
- One API client module. Abort requests on unmount.
- Tests: Vitest for logic and components, one Playwright smoke test for upload, view, report download.
